<title>USA: Armstrong asks for ruling against merger.</title>
<headline>Armstrong asks for ruling against merger.</headline>
<dateline>LANCASTER, Pa. 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Armstrong World Industries Inc said Monday that it formally asked the Ontario and Quebec Securities Commissions to rule against the proposed combination of the flooring businesses of Tarkett AG and Sommer Allibert SA.</p>
<p>Armstrong issued a news release saying the merger, announced on May 28, constitutes an unlawful takeover bid by Tarkett for Domco Inc, which is 57 percent owned by Sommer.  </p>
<p>Canadian securities law requires that takeover bids must normally be extended to all shareholders, Armstrong said.</p>
<p>Tarkett and Sommer have stated publicly that they have no intention of making any offer to Domco minority shareholders, Armstrong said.</p>
